.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-BOOT-MANIFEST 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-boot-manifest
.Nd record what a restore needs that a ZFS archive does not hold
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -host Ar host Op Fl -ssh-key Ar path
.Op Fl -pool Ar pool
.Op Fl -esp-archive Ar file
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Replicating a pool keeps the data and nothing around it.
The EFI system partition is not in the pool; the host id that ZFS records
pool ownership against, the boot environment, the kernel to build an
initramfs for, the disks' shape, the network cards and the Secure Boot
state are facts about the machine, not files in it.
.Nm
writes them down, as one JSON object on standard output, for
.Xr kldload-restore-machine 8
to read with
.Fl -manifest .
.Pp
It reads the local machine, or with
.Fl -host
another over
.Xr ssh 1 .
It captures facts, not secrets: no keys and no passphrases.
Messages go to standard error, so the output can be piped straight to
.Xr jq 1 .
.Pp
The object holds: host name, time, where it was captured from, pool,
.Cm bootfs ,
boot environment, host id, machine id, operating system, running kernel,
ZFS version, Secure Boot state and number of enrolled machine owner keys,
the EFI partition's device, UUID, size in whole MiB and EFI binaries, the
archive's path, the kernels installed, the pool's devices, the network
cards and their MAC addresses,
.Pa /etc/fstab
lines that name a device, and the pool's size and sector shift.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -host Ar host
Read this machine over
.Xr ssh 1 ,
without prompting; exit 2 if it cannot be reached.
.It Fl -ssh-key Ar path
The key for
.Fl -host .
.It Fl -pool Ar pool
The pool to describe; default
.Ql rpool .
It must exist there.
.It Fl -esp-archive Ar file
Also copy the whole EFI partition into
.Ar file ,
as a tar, so a restore can put the old boot path back without a network.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the description at the top of the script and exit 0.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
Captured.
.It 2
The host could not be reached, the pool name was refused, or there is no
such pool; or an unknown argument.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Printed on a kldload desktop on 2026-09-30.
The machine id, MAC addresses and host id are left out here with
.Xr jq 1 .
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-boot-manifest | jq 'del(.machine_id, .nics, .hostid)'
capturing boot manifest for onyx
{
  "hostname": "onyx",
  "captured_at": "2026-09-30T01:13:02-07:00",
  "captured_from": "local",
  "pool": "rpool",
  "bootfs": "rpool/ROOT/onyx",
  "boot_environment": "rpool/ROOT/onyx",
  "os": "kldload (fedora 44)",
  "kernel_running": "7.2.2-300.fc44.x86_64",
  "zfs_version": "2.4.4-1",
  "secure_boot": "SecureBoot enabled",
  "mok_enrolled": "4",
  "esp_device": "/dev/nvme0n1p1",
  "esp_uuid": "23E8-C11A",
  "esp_size": "511M",
  "esp_archive": "",
  "esp_files": [
    "EFI/BOOT/BOOTX64.EFI",
\&...
    "EFI/zbm/mmx64.efi"
  ],
  "kernels_installed": [
    "7.2.2-300.fc44.x86_64"
  ],
  "pool_vdevs": [
    "/dev/nvme0n1p2"
  ],
  "fstab_device_mounts": [
    "UUID=23E8-C11A /boot/efi vfat umask=0077 0 1"
  ],
  "pool_layout": "rpool 1.81T 12",
  "schema": 1
